/// Text is ordered, by code point.
///
/// The relational operators take numbers or a single Char today and refuse a
/// String outright, so 'abc' < 'abd' raises 'Operands must be numbers.'  There
/// is no ordering to preserve and nothing depends on the refusal; it is a gap
/// rather than a decision.
///
/// ⚠️ By code point and nothing else.  Not a collation: not locale-sensitive,
/// no case folding, no normalization.  Two processors have to agree on the
/// answer, and only a mechanical rule can guarantee that -- a locale-aware
/// comparison would make a program's output depend on the machine that ran it.
///
/// Fails with: Operands must be numbers.
///
test 'Text is ordered by code point';
begin
    AssertTrue (Str ('abc') < Str ('abd'));
    AssertTrue (Str ('ab')  < Str ('abc'));
    AssertTrue ('a' < Str ('ab'));
    AssertTrue (Str ('Z') < Str ('a'));
end
